.nh
.TH "PB-INBOX-REQUESTS" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-inbox-requests - List team file requests


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb inbox requests [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List team file requests, one per line: request ID, sender account, number of files,
status and expiry. A request is a sender asking to deliver an exact set of files; approve or
decline it by its request ID. Filter with --owner, --q and --state; the list stops at --limit
unless you pass --all.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	show every item, up to 10000

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for requests

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=50
	show at most this many items (1-200)

.PP
\fB--owner\fP=""
	filter owner: mine, shared, or an authorized account ID

.PP
\fB--q\fP=""
	filter by resource name or ID

.PP
\fB--state\fP=""
	filter by resource state


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb inbox requests
  pb inbox requests --state pending --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-inbox(1)\fP
